WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
Here's why this matters.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:03.871
The organizational units, or O U's,

3
00:00:03.871 --> 00:00:07.925
of an Active Directory forest
were never just folders.

4
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:10.683
That one tree decided who
could manage an object,

5
00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:14.613
which policy reached it, which office
owned it and what it could touch.

6
00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.438
Entra ID has no tree.

7
00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:18.101
Its directory is flat.

8
00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:20.444
So all four of those
jobs have to move into

9
00:00:20.444 --> 00:00:23.063
attributes and the
mechanisms that read them.

10
00:00:23.063 --> 00:00:26.399
One HR-sourced stamp
drives group membership,

11
00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:30.087
delegation, policy, licensing
and drift detection.

12
00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:33.424
If the stamp is wrong, all
five are wrong at once.

13
00:00:33.424 --> 00:00:35.900
So, Module 1, the model.
